{"metadata":{"title":"MXLNumeral.Mode.naturalMinor","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLNumeralV4ModeO12naturalMinoryA2EmF","roleHeading":"Case","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"naturalMinor"}],"symbolKind":"case","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"Natural minor mode.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumeral\/mode\/naturalminor"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumeral","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumeral\/Mode"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"naturalMinor","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumeral\/Mode\/naturalMinor"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumeral/Mode":{"title":"MXLNumeral.Mode","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumeral\/mode","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The numeral-mode type specifies the mode similar to the mode type, but with a restricted set of values. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"different minor values are used to interpret numeral-root values of 6 and 7 when present in a minor key. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"harmonic minor value sharpens the 7 and the melodic minor value sharpens both 6 and 7. If a minor mode is used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"without qualification, either in the mode or numeral-mode elements, natural minor is used."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Mode"}],"kind":"symb